1
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:22,239
Watch out.

2
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:40,079
Lin Ran, it's time to head out.

3
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:41,759
Mom's waiting for you at the door.

4
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:42,719
Okay.

5
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:38,080
Lin Ran

6
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,520
Morning, Ms. Lin.

7
00:02:49,439 --> 00:02:50,000
Morning.

8
00:02:50,759 --> 00:02:51,199
Morning.

9
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,039
I have to get to class.

10
00:02:59,080 --> 00:02:59,680
I'll leave you to it.

11
00:03:01,879 --> 00:03:02,479
Okay.

12
00:03:03,319 --> 00:03:03,719
Your bag.

13
00:03:03,879 --> 00:03:04,280
Right.

14
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,319
Thanks. Thank you.

15
00:03:12,479 --> 00:03:13,360
What did you draw here?

16
00:03:13,879 --> 00:03:15,199
I wanted to draw a bouquet of flowers.

17
00:03:15,199 --> 00:03:17,960
I just mixed a random color on here.

18
00:03:18,599 --> 00:03:19,159
Looks good.

19
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,919
What's wrong? Did you run into a problem?

20
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,960
I spilled paint on it.

21
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,080
That's alright.

22
00:03:53,319 --> 00:03:54,360
Just treat it as

23
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:56,400
a pattern on this little hedgehog.

24
00:03:56,599 --> 00:03:58,360
Do hedgehogs have patterns on them?

25
00:03:59,039 --> 00:04:01,120
It does if you want it to.

26
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,479
Use your imagination. Just paint it like this.

27
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:05,759
You can use all these colors.

28
00:04:05,759 --> 00:04:07,599
Can this be an apple too?

29
00:04:08,319 --> 00:04:09,080
Yes.

30
00:04:15,319 --> 00:04:16,240
What's wrong?

31
00:04:16,439 --> 00:04:19,120
She got some paint in her eye.

32
00:04:19,879 --> 00:04:21,319
Don't touch it. Let me see. Your hands are dirty.

33
00:04:21,319 --> 00:04:22,360
Let me see. Let me see.

34
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,879
Open it gently.

35
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,560
Ultimately, it really is my fault.

36
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:41,480
Xiao Mei got paint in her eyes today,

37
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,399
and I really couldn't keep an eye on her at the time.

38
00:04:43,399 --> 00:04:44,480
Because the other kids

39
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,160
were also asking me to look at their work.

40
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:48,240
But I'm not making excuses for myself.

41
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,639
It was definitely my oversight.

42
00:04:51,079 --> 00:04:52,279
When I was little, I also often got paint

43
00:04:52,279 --> 00:04:53,040
in my eyes.

44
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,160
But look, my eyes are perfectly fine now, right?

45
00:04:55,639 --> 00:04:57,600
But I guess it's still my fault.

46
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,439
So I wanted to apologize.

47
00:05:00,839 --> 00:05:01,759
It's fine.

48
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:04,959
Xiao Mei used to get her eyes in chili a lot before.

49
00:05:04,959 --> 00:05:05,480
No.

50
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,800
Get chili in her eyes.

51
00:05:08,199 --> 00:05:08,920
It's okay.

52
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,519
Besides, the doctor also said

53
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:11,439
it's nothing serious.

54
00:05:11,759 --> 00:05:12,879
A simple treatment is all it takes.

55
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,000
That's good then.

56
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,279
He's playing really well.

57
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:42,360
He's on a 23-game winning streak.

58
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,879
He must be a pro.

59
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,240
Want to play a round with me?

60
00:06:05,279 --> 00:06:05,839
Yes.

61
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,079
I've already sent you the documents.

62
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,199
I'd like to apply for online verification.

63
00:06:09,639 --> 00:06:10,480
60 kilograms.

64
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,680
30 barbell power snatches.

65
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,759
No problem. I can do it.

66
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:55,720
Lin Ran

67
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:02,199
All done, Sister Chun.

68
00:07:02,639 --> 00:07:04,199
See if you need any touch-ups.

69
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,319
You did a great job.

70
00:07:08,319 --> 00:07:09,160
It looks perfect.

71
00:07:10,279 --> 00:07:10,879
Wait.

72
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:12,839
What's your name?

73
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:14,399
I'm Lin Ran.

74
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,639
Too high, too high.

75
00:07:27,639 --> 00:07:28,680
You're blocking Sister Chun's face.

76
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:29,600
Cut, cut, cut!

77
00:07:32,279 --> 00:07:33,160
Take this ring...

78
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,680
Come on, let's measure the distance again.

79
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:35,319
Sister Chun, look.

80
00:07:35,319 --> 00:07:36,079
Can you reach it?

81
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:38,160
Almost. You can come a bit closer.

82
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:38,839
Just about, right?

83
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,639
Can you stretch your arm out a bit more?

84
00:07:40,639 --> 00:07:41,399
Okay, otherwise it's out of reach.

85
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:42,399
The actor will reach out to grab it.

86
00:07:42,639 --> 00:07:43,120
Okay.

87
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:43,519
Good.

88
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:44,920
Let's try it again.

89
00:07:44,959 --> 00:07:46,199
The camera wasn't quite right just now either.

90
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,240
Sister Chun is good here.

91
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:47,879
Come on, let's do it again.

92
00:07:47,879 --> 00:07:48,720
Come on, once more.

93
00:07:48,839 --> 00:07:49,800
Remember this position.

94
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,319
Thanks, Sister Chun.

95
00:07:54,319 --> 00:07:55,000
Let's do another take.

96
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,240
Come on, get ready.

97
00:07:56,319 --> 00:07:57,120
Okay, let's go.

98
00:07:57,399 --> 00:07:58,199
Get ready to shoot.

99
00:07:58,199 --> 00:07:58,839
Rolling!

100
00:07:59,120 --> 00:07:59,759
Action!

101
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:00,720
Car moving!

102
00:08:04,439 --> 00:08:05,240
Okay, hand it over.

103
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,079
Cut, cut!

104
00:08:11,439 --> 00:08:12,800
Are you not going to hand over the ring?

105
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,199
Are you reluctant to give it to her?

106
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:15,680
Switch him out. Switch him out!

107
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,560
Let me do it. I'll do it.

108
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:17,600
Dongdong, come down. Come down.

109
00:08:17,879 --> 00:08:18,439
Come measure the distance.

110
00:08:18,439 --> 00:08:19,199
His arms are a bit longer.

111
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:20,199
Make sure you hand the ring all the way over.

112
00:08:20,199 --> 00:08:21,600
Otherwise it looks like you don't want to hand it over.

113
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:21,959
Okay.

114
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:23,480
Let's check the positions first, or else...

115
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:24,759
Right, right. Let's set the positions beforehand.

116
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:25,560
Is this okay?

117
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,120
It's fine, right?

118
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:26,399
Okay.

119
00:08:26,399 --> 00:08:26,759
Okay, thanks everyone.

120
00:08:26,759 --> 00:08:27,639
Let's try it once more.

121
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:43,600
I do.

122
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:48,120
Cut!

123
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:48,879
Good.

124
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:49,879
Hold on a sec.

125
00:08:49,879 --> 00:08:50,639
Just give us a second.

126
00:08:51,399 --> 00:08:52,039
Yezi.

127
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,519
Are we done shooting for today?

128
00:08:53,519 --> 00:08:54,519
Okay, let me check.

129
00:08:56,759 --> 00:08:57,919
Director, we're all done.

130
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,159
Good work, everyone.

131
00:09:01,159 --> 00:09:02,000
Alright, Director. Bye.

132
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:02,639
Bye, bye.

133
00:09:02,639 --> 00:09:03,480
See you tomorrow, Sister Chun.

134
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,360
Okay, see you tomorrow.

135
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,039
Alright.

136
00:09:09,159 --> 00:09:10,159
Good work, Sister Chun.

137
00:09:10,159 --> 00:09:11,200
Good work, Sister Chun.

138
00:09:11,279 --> 00:09:12,360
Good work, everyone.

139
00:09:14,519 --> 00:09:15,879
We'll see you tomorrow, Sister Chun.

140
00:09:15,879 --> 00:09:16,679
See you tomorrow.

141
00:09:36,879 --> 00:09:37,480
You're back.

142
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,039
You're still awake?

143
00:09:45,759 --> 00:09:47,200
What am I even saying?

144
00:09:53,279 --> 00:09:54,279
Are you in a rush to sleep?

145
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,559
I'm not in a rush to sleep.

146
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,480
I wanted to chat with everyone.

147
00:10:00,879 --> 00:10:01,720
Just a casual chat.

148
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:03,559
Let's talk.

149
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,080
Alright.

150
00:10:05,879 --> 00:10:06,480
Have a drink first.

151
00:10:16,039 --> 00:10:16,840
What?

152
00:10:30,919 --> 00:10:33,559
I said, I want more time.

153
00:10:33,559 --> 00:10:34,879
But not to take over completely.

154
00:10:34,879 --> 00:10:37,080
Just a little more than before.

155
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,679
Like 12 hours.

156
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,360
That's a bit much, huh.

157
00:10:43,799 --> 00:10:44,480
Then...

158
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,120
11.

159
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,279
Ten.

160
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,759
Just... just ten.

161
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,759
Ten hours.

162
00:10:51,879 --> 00:10:53,000
Are you kidding me?

163
00:10:53,559 --> 00:10:54,120
Yeah.

164
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:55,720
You've never said this before.

165
00:10:56,159 --> 00:10:59,000
Are you in some kind of trouble?

166
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:00,159
I...

167
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:01,080
Whatever trouble you're in,

168
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,480
you can't drag all of us down!

169
00:11:02,799 --> 00:11:03,960
What do you mean, drag us down?

170
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,720
That's a really harsh thing to say.

171
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:06,279
That's...

172
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,840
You're being a bit too heartless.

173
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:08,639
Me, heartless?

174
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:10,519
Stealing our time isn't heartless?

175
00:11:10,519 --> 00:11:11,279
I'm not stealing it.

176
00:11:11,279 --> 00:11:12,879
I'm just trying to discuss this nicely!

177
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,200
You call this discussing?

178
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:16,919
Calm down, calm down.

179
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:17,720
Where are you going?

180
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,799
I'm not done talking!

181
00:11:19,039 --> 00:11:19,679
Get back here!

182
00:11:30,679 --> 00:11:31,919
It's my right to begin with.

183
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:33,240
What right do you have?

184
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:34,559
What right do I have?

185
00:11:34,879 --> 00:11:36,080
All your time belongs to me.

186
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,200
You tell me what right I have.

187
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:48,840
I... I didn't phrase that right.

188
00:11:50,519 --> 00:11:51,600
That's not what I meant.

189
00:11:52,279 --> 00:11:53,639
Other than when we sleep,

190
00:11:54,039 --> 00:11:55,519
every day, each of us gets

191
00:11:55,519 --> 00:11:57,000
four hours of body time.

192
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:58,600
You said it yourself.

193
00:11:58,759 --> 00:11:59,799
It's always been this way.

194
00:12:01,639 --> 00:12:02,279
Exactly.

195
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:13,240
And

196
00:12:13,639 --> 00:12:15,480
we've always kept this agreement.

197
00:12:17,559 --> 00:12:18,120
Right?

198
00:12:22,639 --> 00:12:23,840
I know it's not easy for everyone,

199
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:25,200
and everyone is sticking to the agreement.

200
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:29,799
But I really have a special situation this time.

201
00:12:31,519 --> 00:12:32,519
A special situation?

202
00:12:32,919 --> 00:12:34,360
You're not the only one with a special situation.

203
00:12:36,879 --> 00:12:37,840
You play pretty well.

204
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,000
You're not bad yourself.

205
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,720
Right, I forgot to introduce myself.

206
00:12:41,919 --> 00:12:42,559
I'm Lyu Sheng.

207
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:45,919
You're the legendary Lyu?

208
00:12:46,639 --> 00:12:47,600
You own this internet cafe?

209
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:48,759
Yeah.

210
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:49,679
Hello.

211
00:12:49,679 --> 00:12:50,200
Nice to meet you.

212
00:12:50,639 --> 00:12:51,200
Sorry about that.

213
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,840
I want to invite you to join my team.

214
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:54,799
What?

215
00:12:55,279 --> 00:12:56,639
There's an offline tournament next month.

216
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:57,720
I know.

217
00:12:57,720 --> 00:12:58,919
The WPT.

218
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,720
But one of our players had an emergency.

219
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,039
So we need a substitute.

220
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:04,960
I'm bringing in another sub tomorrow.

221
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:05,840
You two will play a match.

222
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:07,320
The winner joins the team directly.

223
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,639
Tomorrow morning at 9:00.

224
00:13:09,759 --> 00:13:11,279
The time might be an issue.

225
00:13:12,159 --> 00:13:12,720
Maybe

226
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,559
we could do it after 10:00?

227
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,399
The thing is, the other sub is a foreigner.

228
00:13:16,639 --> 00:13:18,200
His flight back home is at 2:00 PM tomorrow.

229
00:13:18,559 --> 00:13:19,799
So we probably can't change the time.

230
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:21,799
And then?

231
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,600
There is no "and then."

232
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:26,320
I have to find a place to hand the body over to you.

233
00:13:27,879 --> 00:13:30,639
A few minutes wouldn't hurt, honestly.

234
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:31,919
No way.

235
00:13:32,679 --> 00:13:33,519
A deal is a deal.

236
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,639
I don't want to cause trouble for everyone.

237
00:13:38,279 --> 00:13:39,080
I'm sorry.

238
00:13:39,399 --> 00:13:40,639
I didn't know about your situation.

239
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:42,080
Well, now you know.

240
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:44,679
Will you give up your time tomorrow morning for me?

241
00:13:48,879 --> 00:13:49,600
I knew it.

242
00:13:53,159 --> 00:13:54,000
Actually,

243
00:13:55,159 --> 00:13:56,080
I also wanted

244
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,120
to discuss something with you.

245
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:00,639
Discuss what?

246
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:02,559
I wanted to say...

247
00:14:02,879 --> 00:14:03,799
I got the email.

248
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:05,039
I need to be there at 7:00 PM tomorrow.

249
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:06,960
I also wanted to ask,

250
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:09,120
is there any way I can compete earlier?

251
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:11,840
Just... just like the online matches,

252
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,559
I could finish all the events,

253
00:14:13,559 --> 00:14:15,039
and compare my times with the other players.

254
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:22,360
I understand.

255
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:24,679
I'm really sorry

256
00:14:24,879 --> 00:14:25,600
for the trouble.

257
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:30,960
No.

258
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,679
If you break the rules like this,

259
00:14:32,759 --> 00:14:34,120
things will definitely get messy.

260
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:37,600
I'm sorry.

261
00:14:39,039 --> 00:14:39,720
Tomorrow won't work.

262
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:41,759
Sister Chun, you wanted to see me?

263
00:14:42,679 --> 00:14:43,360
Have a seat.

264
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:46,519
Here's the thing.

265
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,000
Lately,

266
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,120
my schedule is packed.

267
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,759
I want to hire a personal makeup artist.

268
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:52,200
And I think you're really good.

269
00:14:53,639 --> 00:14:54,080
Sister Chun,

270
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,639
I'm just here to help out temporarily.

271
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:56,840
I know.

272
00:14:57,279 --> 00:14:58,240
But I see a lot of potential in you.

273
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:00,159
Thank you, Sister Chun.

274
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,240
But...

275
00:15:03,879 --> 00:15:05,639
I might have some scheduling issues.

276
00:15:07,159 --> 00:15:09,519
That's okay, you don't have to answer right away.

277
00:15:09,799 --> 00:15:11,440
Take some time to think about it.

278
00:15:12,039 --> 00:15:13,279
I have a shoot tomorrow night too.

279
00:15:13,799 --> 00:15:14,919
You can let me know then.

280
00:15:16,279 --> 00:15:17,240
So, as you all know,

281
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,360
because of this time issue,

282
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:21,879
over the years,

283
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,919
I've only been able to take odd jobs.

284
00:15:24,399 --> 00:15:25,000
Right.

285
00:15:25,879 --> 00:15:27,080
We all know your skills.

286
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:28,720
It's a bit of a waste of your talent.

287
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:32,600
I'm sorry.

288
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:35,480
I've been too selfish.

289
00:15:38,159 --> 00:15:38,679
No.

290
00:15:39,919 --> 00:15:41,440
If you were truly selfish,

291
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,480
we wouldn't even exist.

292
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,960
Yeah, exactly.

293
00:15:49,559 --> 00:15:50,559
You're the host.

294
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:52,799
You don't have to share your time with us at all.

295
00:15:54,559 --> 00:15:55,200
That's not true.

296
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:57,720
I have to do this.

297
00:15:58,799 --> 00:15:59,840
Because I need you guys.

298
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:04,720
I'm ordinary and mediocre.

299
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:08,919
I need you to help me realize my worth.

300
00:16:24,399 --> 00:16:25,440
Did the power go out?

301
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:27,480
Let's go check.

302
00:16:29,879 --> 00:16:30,639
It's back on.

303
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,039
Probably old wiring.

304
00:16:32,039 --> 00:16:32,960
I'll get someone to fix it tomorrow.

305
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,000
Lin... Where's Lin Ran?

306
00:16:36,039 --> 00:16:36,840
Lin Ran!

307
00:16:37,679 --> 00:16:38,360
Lin Ran!

308
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:39,360
Ranran!

309
00:16:42,039 --> 00:16:42,600
Ranran!

310
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:45,159
Lin Ran!

311
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:46,799
Lin Ran!

312
00:16:48,279 --> 00:16:48,879
Any sign of her?

313
00:16:48,879 --> 00:16:49,480
No.

314
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:52,759
Not here!
